    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d815">

                <pb facs="0773" n="657" sameAs="frus:frus1912/pg657"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 741.8215/44.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The American Ambassador to Great Britain to the
                        Secretary of State</hi>.</head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram.—Paraphrase.]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">American Embassy</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">London</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1912-04-12">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 12, 1912</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>Replying to my request for leniency in dealing with the Liberian boundary
                    troubles, the Foreign Office has assured me that the British Government will
                    exercise all possible forbearance. The Governor of Sierra Leone has been
                    instructed to suspend action until he receives further instructions.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Reid.</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
